From 944d98ec787120938d89238cd91fdc8416a712d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruben Herold <ruben@puettmann.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:15:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] T9499: ppp: do not close the shared fd of a non-dev ppp
 session early

destablish_ppp() closes unit_fd after the session cleanup since
2fc996b (T9238). For a non-dev ppp session (VPP) unit_fd is the same
file descriptor as ppp->fd and the channel handler, which is
unregistered afterwards in destroy_ppp_channel(). The handler then runs
epoll_ctl(EPOLL_CTL_DEL) on a closed descriptor, EBADF makes triton
call abort(), and accel-pppd dies with every other session.

Do not close unit_fd for a non-dev ppp session, destroy_ppp_channel()
takes care of the descriptor as before.

Signed-off-by: Ruben Herold <ruben@puettmann.net>
---
 accel-pppd/ppp/ppp.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/accel-pppd/ppp/ppp.c b/accel-pppd/ppp/ppp.c
index 235b4b62..52dd2fc3 100644
--- a/accel-pppd/ppp/ppp.c
+++ b/accel-pppd/ppp/ppp.c
@@ -368,7 +368,11 @@ static void destablish_ppp(struct ppp_t *ppp)
 	 * radattr removal) has finished, so the kernel cannot give the same
 	 * unit index (and thus ifname) to a new session while cleanup still
 	 * references the ifname. */
-	if (!uc)
+	if (!uc
+#ifdef HAVE_SESSION_HOOKS
+	    && !is_non_dev_ppp
+#endif /* HAVE_SESSION_HOOKS */
+	    )
 		close(ppp->unit_fd);
 
 	ppp->unit_fd = -1;
